<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34107" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pătĭbĭlis</span></b> ,
			e, adj.
		patior. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Pass.</i>, <i>supportable</i>, <i>endurable</i> (syn.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tolerabilis, ferendus): patibiles et dolores et
					labores putandi (sunt),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Tusc. 4, 23, 51</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>Sensitive</i>, <i>passible</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">patibilem naturam habere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					N. D. 3, 12, 29</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>Suffering</i>, <i>passive</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alterum elementum activum, alterum patibile,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lact. 2, 9 <i>med.</i></span></i>
			</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>